WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.081 --> 00:00:01.345
Good evening!

2
00:00:01.345 --> 00:00:02.525
(audience applauding)

3
00:00:02.525 --> 00:00:03.858
You're too kind!

4
00:00:05.403 --> 00:00:08.160
I'm following the president, or something.

5
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.074
Oh, this is so exciting.

6
00:00:10.074 --> 00:00:12.290
Big week, big week, ladies and gentlemen.

7
00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.245
The new iPhone is out, yeah.

8
00:00:15.245 --> 00:00:17.907
I have a love hate relationship with my iPhone.

9
00:00:17.907 --> 00:00:20.005
I basically think that smartphones

10
00:00:20.005 --> 00:00:22.502
have got too smart for their own good.

11
00:00:22.502 --> 00:00:25.382
I miss having a dumb phone.

12
00:00:25.382 --> 00:00:28.755
Do you know the phone I miss every day of my life?

13
00:00:28.755 --> 00:00:30.477
The Nokia 3310

14
00:00:30.477 --> 00:00:31.310
(audience cheering)

15
00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:32.668
Oh!

16
00:00:32.668 --> 00:00:34.454
That was a phone!

17
00:00:34.454 --> 00:00:36.521
Screw the iPhone with all of its apps,

18
00:00:36.521 --> 00:00:38.727
and its maps, and this GPS crap!

19
00:00:38.727 --> 00:00:41.634
The Nokia 3310 gave a man all he needed,

20
00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:45.801
stopwatch, calculator, and Snake, screw anything else!

21
00:00:47.502 --> 00:00:49.076
I loved that phone.

22
00:00:49.076 --> 00:00:52.219
And there was no pretension with the 3310 as well.

23
00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:54.603
Predictive text messaging on the 3310.

24
00:00:54.603 --> 00:00:56.782
Oh, it was bliss, do you remember that?

25
00:00:56.782 --> 00:00:59.775
If you tried to type in a word to the 3310

26
00:00:59.775 --> 00:01:02.279
that was more than four letters long,

27
00:01:02.279 --> 00:01:04.488
it would just give up.

28
00:01:04.488 --> 00:01:07.881
"Yeah, you want to use fancy pants language like that,

29
00:01:07.881 --> 00:01:10.052
you're on your own, mate!"

30
00:01:10.052 --> 00:01:11.152
Not the iPhone.

31
00:01:11.152 --> 00:01:13.593
Where did the iPhone get its vocabulary?

32
00:01:13.593 --> 00:01:16.017
It doesn't matter what you type in, A-N,

33
00:01:16.017 --> 00:01:17.963
"Did you mean androgynous?"

34
00:01:17.963 --> 00:01:19.271
"No!

35
00:01:19.271 --> 00:01:20.470
"I meant and!"

36
00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.470
(audience laughing)

37
00:01:24.836 --> 00:01:26.234
It's very nice to be here.

38
00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:27.323
It's very nice to be here in New York.

39
00:01:27.323 --> 00:01:29.441
It's very nice to be anywhere right now, yeah.

40
00:01:29.441 --> 00:01:32.441
(audience cheering)

41
00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:35.422
Back home, we're going through

42
00:01:35.422 --> 00:01:38.743
quite a nasty divorce right now, called Brexit.

43
00:01:38.743 --> 00:01:40.849
And I want to take this opportunity,

44
00:01:40.849 --> 00:01:43.613
on behalf of my nation, to thank you, America.

45
00:01:43.613 --> 00:01:46.992
I want to thank you from the bottom of our hearts.

46
00:01:46.992 --> 00:01:48.701
We owe you a huge debt of thanks

47
00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:50.607
because we woke up after Brexit,

48
00:01:50.607 --> 00:01:51.632
and I'm not gonna lie, we thought,

49
00:01:51.632 --> 00:01:53.878
"That is it, we are screwed."

50
00:01:53.878 --> 00:01:55.849
"We are now gonna be the most

51
00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:58.730
ridiculed nation on the planet."

52
00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:01.825
And then, last November, you guys went, "Hold my beer."

53
00:02:01.825 --> 00:02:04.636
(audience cheering)

54
00:02:04.636 --> 00:02:05.469
Thank you.

55
00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:13.268
There are some angry people in this country right now.

56
00:02:13.268 --> 00:02:14.492
Oh my God, you're living in a country

57
00:02:14.492 --> 00:02:16.829
where there were people that boycotted

58
00:02:16.829 --> 00:02:19.027
Disney's Beauty and the Beast

59
00:02:19.027 --> 00:02:21.856
because it had a gay character in it.

60
00:02:21.856 --> 00:02:24.586
Yeah, the Christian right were up in arms,

61
00:02:24.586 --> 00:02:27.698
a gay character in Beauty and the Beast.

62
00:02:27.698 --> 00:02:30.821
They were like, "It's against God's law."

63
00:02:30.821 --> 00:02:33.810
The film is about a girl shagging a buffalo.

64
00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:36.810
(audience laughing)

65
00:02:42.001 --> 00:02:43.962
I love Disney, I love Disney, but I've been tested.

66
00:02:43.962 --> 00:02:46.203
My love of Disney has been tested this year.

67
00:02:46.203 --> 00:02:48.150
Earlier on this year, I stayed over here.

68
00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.608
They messed up my hotel booking.

69
00:02:49.608 --> 00:02:52.216
And I had to stay in the Disney Hotel

70
00:02:52.216 --> 00:02:56.197
for a month of my life as a grown man.

71
00:02:56.197 --> 00:02:59.595
I nearly turned into Jack Nicholson from the Shining.

72
00:02:59.595 --> 00:03:02.511
Because it is too much Disney at the Disney Hotel.

73
00:03:02.511 --> 00:03:04.291
There's Disney music in every elevator.

74
00:03:04.291 --> 00:03:06.866
There's Disney characters on the walls and the bed linen.

75
00:03:06.866 --> 00:03:08.905
Disney characters embroidered onto all

76
00:03:08.905 --> 00:03:10.742
of the towels in the bathroom.

77
00:03:10.742 --> 00:03:11.575
Yes!

78
00:03:11.575 --> 00:03:15.693
I know that sounds sweet, until you're drying your testicles

79
00:03:15.693 --> 00:03:18.614
on the face of the old man from Up.

80
00:03:18.614 --> 00:03:19.524
Just there,

81
00:03:19.524 --> 00:03:20.604
(audience laughing)

82
00:03:20.604 --> 00:03:24.090
in the bathroom, teabagging a grieving senior citizen.

83
00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:27.840
You're like, "Oh, I'm sorry about your wife."

84
00:03:31.582 --> 00:03:34.268
Disney characters that work at the hotel

85
00:03:34.268 --> 00:03:37.194
as members of staff, that by company policy,

86
00:03:37.194 --> 00:03:38.844
are not allowed to break character

87
00:03:38.844 --> 00:03:41.428
at any point during your stay.

88
00:03:41.428 --> 00:03:44.927
Have you got any idea how annoying that is?

89
00:03:44.927 --> 00:03:48.093
You check in, and Goofy's on reception.

90
00:03:48.093 --> 00:03:51.856
Walk into the restaurant, Donald Duck's doing teppenyaki.

91
00:03:51.856 --> 00:03:54.230
I can pinpoint, though, the exact moment

92
00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.909
that my childhood died.

93
00:03:55.909 --> 00:03:57.517
I'd been there for two weeks.

94
00:03:57.517 --> 00:04:01.100
I was in my room, I was tired, I was alone.

95
00:04:01.982 --> 00:04:04.378
I called down to the front desk,

96
00:04:04.378 --> 00:04:07.201
Mickey Mouse answers the phone,

97
00:04:07.201 --> 00:04:11.238
"Hey, hey, hey, buddy, what can I do for you today?"

98
00:04:11.238 --> 00:04:12.071
"Mickey,

99
00:04:13.145 --> 00:04:16.787
I need to activate the porn channels on my TV."

100
00:04:16.787 --> 00:04:19.787
(audience laughing)

101
00:04:22.768 --> 00:04:24.922
Inner child's dead.

102
00:04:24.922 --> 00:04:26.373
You don't want this interaction.

103
00:04:26.373 --> 00:04:28.662
These are your childhood heroes.

104
00:04:28.662 --> 00:04:30.996
Arguing with Simba at the front desk

105
00:04:30.996 --> 00:04:33.008
about your itemized bill,

106
00:04:33.008 --> 00:04:35.312
"Listen mate, I want to speak with someone more senior.

107
00:04:35.312 --> 00:04:36.920
"Fetch me

108
00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:37.753
Mufasa!"

109
00:04:37.753 --> 00:04:40.022
(audience laughing)

110
00:04:40.022 --> 00:04:41.788
Ladies and gentlemen, thank you very much!

111
00:04:41.788 --> 00:04:44.371
I am Jack Whitehall, goodnight.

